---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Templates
permalink: /demos/
description: Complete, sellable website templates by industry — each one a working site with a real back office, not a mockup.
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---

<section class="pagehead">
  <div class="hero__grid-bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="shell" style="position:relative;z-index:1">
    <span class="label label--signal">Template library</span>
    <h1 class="h1" style="margin-top:1rem">Templates</h1>
    <p class="lede" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
      Finished websites for specific trades. Each one runs its own booking or
      intake flow into a working back office, so you can click the whole loop
      before deciding anything.
    </p>

    <div class="pagehead__meta">
      <span class="label label--faint">{{ collections.demoTemplates | length }} available</span>
      <span class="label label--faint">Rebranded from one file</span>
      <span class="label label--faint">Sold outright, hosted anywhere</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="eyebrow">
      <span class="label">Available now</span>
      <span class="eyebrow__rule"></span>
      <span class="label label--plain label--faint" data-for-note hidden></span>
    </div>

    <div class="cards">
      {% for item in collections.demoTemplates %}
        {% set meta = item.data.demoMeta %}
        <article class="card" data-reveal data-reveal-delay="{{ loop.index0 * 70 }}">
          <a class="tpl__thumb" href="{{ item.url }}" data-demo-link
             aria-label="Open the {{ meta.name }} template">
            <img src="{{ meta.thumbnail }}" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
          </a>

          <div class="card__body">
            <div class="tpl__row">
              <span class="label label--signal">{{ meta.industry }}</span>
              <span class="tpl__status">{{ meta.status }}</span>
            </div>

            <h2 class="h3" style="margin-top:.9rem">{{ meta.name }}</h2>
            <p class="body body--sm" style="margin-top:.75rem">{{ meta.blurb }}</p>
          </div>

          <div class="card__foot">
            <span class="label label--plain label--faint">{{ meta.pages }} pages</span>
            <a class="link" href="{{ item.url }}" data-demo-link>
              Open the demo <span class="btn__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
      {% else %}
        <p class="body">No templates published yet.</p>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band band--dark section">
  <div class="shell">
    <div class="split">
      <div class="split__lead">
        <h2 class="h2">How these are sold</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split__body">
        <p class="lede" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">
          You buy the template outright. I rebrand it to your practice or firm,
          point it at your domain, and hand over the whole repository.
        </p>
        <p class="body" style="margin-bottom:2rem">
          Every name, address, price and record in a template lives in a single
          data file, so rebranding is an edit rather than a rebuild. Back-office
          features run on local storage in the demo; on a live build they run
          against a real database.
        </p>
        <a class="btn" href="/start/">
          Ask about a template <span class="btn__glyph" aria-hidden="true">&#8599;</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  /* /demos/?for=Ridgeway%20Family%20Care forwards the name to every demo link
     as ?prospect=, so a personalised catalogue link personalises the demos. */
  (function () {
    try {
      var who = new URLSearchParams(location.search).get('for');
      if (!who) return;
      who = who.slice(0, 60).trim();
      if (!who) return;

      document.querySelectorAll('[data-demo-link]').forEach(function (a) {
        var u = new URL(a.getAttribute('href'), location.origin);
        u.searchParams.set('prospect', who);
        a.setAttribute('href', u.pathname + u.search);
      });

      var note = document.querySelector('[data-for-note]');
      if (note) {
        note.textContent = 'Prepared for ' + who;
        note.hidden = false;
      }
    } catch (e) {}
  })();
</script>
